commit f94543c3f498a859f82e23e2b63d1d03d7c6f452
Author: pose-fix <pose-fix@local>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 08:12:25 2026 +0000

    fix(optimizer): judge pose-opt-line outliers on the residual at the current pose
    
    PoseOptimizationWithLine() read chi2() straight out of g2o's cached _error.
    Edges parked at level 1 are excluded from initializeOptimization(0), so
    optimize() never recomputes their residual: a line that the current pose has
    already pulled back inside the threshold stayed an outlier for the remaining
    three rounds and never re-entered the graph. Each of the four judging loops
    (vpEdgesMono, vpEdgesStereo, vpEdgesLineMono, vpEdgesLineStereo) now calls
    computeError() first, and a non-finite chi2 counts as an outlier.
    
    Thresholds, outlier flags, setLevel(), nBad and the robust-kernel schedule are
    unchanged; the point-only PoseOptimization() and everything outside these four
    loops are untouched.

